WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
Here's a French sentence about work:

2
00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:05.250
«Le chômage touche surtout
les jeunes.» Word for word,

3
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.990
that's 'The unemployment
mainly affects the young'.

4
00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:11.390
English doesn't want either 'the'.

5
00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:15.790
In class: «J'ai levé la
main.» I raised… the hand?

6
00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:19.640
Then: «Elle est
infirmière.» She is… nurse.

7
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.650
Where did English 'a' go?

8
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:25.180
So when does French add a little
word that English leaves out,

9
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.820
and when does it drop one English needs?

10
00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:31.250
In this mission, you'll fill
Mission D1's empty boxes

11
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:34.870
and send «de» through
Mission D2's switchboard.

12
00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.020
Then you'll test agreements
in Mission I1 and feed

13
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:41.080
verbs into Mission D3's noun machine.

14
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.300
Your mission: crack when
French adds a little word,

15
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.290
when it drops one, and why.
